  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scoping mission on EU support to the European Management University in Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The objective of this scoping mission is to assess the rationale and strategic orientation for a potential new EU intervention to support the establishment of the European Management University (EMU) in Vietnam. The specific objective of the assignment is to provide an independent assessment of: 1.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;the relevance of the establishment of the EMU in Vietnam, taking due consideration of, but not limited to, the current higher education landscape in Vietnam, the labour market demand and the country&#xbf;s development ambition. 2.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;the necessary conditions, key challenges and arrangements required for the establishment of the EMU in Vietnam. 3.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;the validity and viability of the latest EMU proposal, which will be shared with the contractor. 4.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;the possible value added and role of the EU in this project, and in which modality(ies)/set up. In conducting the assignment, the Contractor shall duly take into account the cross-cutting objectives of the EC, higher priority will be given to climate change and persons with disabilities. The global and specific objectives shall clarify that all EU funded actions must promote the cross-cutting objectives of the EC: environment and climate change, rights based approach, persons with disability, indigenous peoples and gender equality.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
